# Batch files are parsed by cmd.exe, which reads them line by line and is not
# reliable on LF-only input: a label or a multi-line block can be mis-parsed,
# and the failure is silent. Check them out with CRLF on every platform so a
# fixture that works today cannot break when someone adds a goto to it.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts are the mirror image: CRLF in a #! script makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter with a trailing carriage return and report the
# file as not found.
*.sh text eol=lf
